<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF wins Indonesian navy order.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF wins Indonesian navy order.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>French defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF said on Friday it had won an order worth $50 million to supply mission systems to the Indonesian navy.</p>
<p>Six Indonesian CN 212 naval aircraft will be equipped with Thomson-CSF's Amascos mission systems under a contract signed in Paris on Thursday, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The systems incorporate the Ocean Master maritime surveillance radar from Thomson-CSF and Dasa, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
